findings.description:
PROTOCOL §12 l.485 and DATA_CONTRACT l.191 say r4_gate_c --counts 'recomputes the four clauses independently of excluded_by'. _overlaps uses:
- AD.an_links() (l.48);
- AD._canon (l.52);
- the an3_records copy_group column, built from the same copy_group_map().
The unit test (tests/test_slots_c.py l.62-70) does the same. Both only re-check excluded_by's boolean OR. A wrong link map would pass both checks with 0 overlaps: for example a fingerprint or threshold different from the project's ECFP r2/2048 @ 0.7 rule, or a canonicalisation mismatch. The 0-in-248 result therefore does not independently confirm the linked-chemotype clause.
